  "id": "5450f7b2-f64a-4ec3-b604-06adbf831dc2",
  "title": "Delhi Protests: Supreme Court Dismisses Plea Against Metro Services Amid CJP Controversy",
  "summary": "The Supreme Court dismissed a plea against the Delhi Metro, Delhi Police, and Union Home Secretary for violating the October 9 order to prevent a complete ban on metro and train services during the CJP protest. The court also ruled against influencers for jokes related to the riots.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court dismissed a plea against the Delhi Metro, Delhi Police, and Union Home Secretary for violating the October 9 order to prevent a complete ban on metro and train services during the CJP protest.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The court ruled against influencers for jokes related to the riots.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The Supreme Court ordered that people gathering peacefully should not be illegally detained, as it issued a notice to the Centre on a plea seeking contempt proceedings for alleged violation of the court's direction to ensure that there is no 'complete prohibition' on metro and train services.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
